{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.SchurWeylMassDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.SchurWeylMassDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_additive_wedderburn_missing_partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_additive_wedderburn_missing_partitions","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L124-L129","doc":"**`additive_wedderburn_missing_partitions_axiom` is false.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_a_eq_one_three_channels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_a_eq_one_three_channels","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L118-L122","doc":"**`a_eq_one_three_channels_axiom` is false.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.emptyDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.emptyDecomposition","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L109-L116","doc":"An instance whose partition list is empty.  `decomposition` holds\nbecause the empty sum is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Decomposition: trace equals weighted sum over partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The Markov trace of the atomic braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.partitions","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The list of partitions of `3A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.q","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.atomicBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.atomicBraid","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The atomic braid as an element of `H_{3A}(q)` (opaque). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SchurWeylMassDecomposition","kind":"class","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L50-L76","doc":"**Schur–Weyl mass decomposition.**\n\nFor an atomic braid `𝒜 ∈ H_{3A}(q)` on `3A` strands, the\nMarkov trace decomposes over partitions of `3A`:\n\n  tr_M(𝒜) = Σ_{λ ⊢ 3A} w_λ(q) · χ^λ(𝒜)\n\nThis is the exact Wedderburn decomposition; the engine's\nadditive-H₃-per-generator approximation drops all partitions\nthat are not concatenations of three-row blocks.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `thm:wedderburn-mass-formula`,\n     `prop:three-parameters-wedderburn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.schurWeylWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.schurWeylWeight","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Schur–Weyl weight: `w_λ(q) = s_λ(q, q⁻¹) / H_q(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spechtCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spechtCharacter","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The Specht-module character of the atomic braid.  Concrete\nmodel: returns 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.schurAtQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.schurAtQ","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L38-L39","doc":"The Schur function `s_λ(q, q⁻¹)`.  Content-bearing via `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qHookProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qHookProduct","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L31-L36","doc":"The q-hook product `H_q(λ) = ∏_{x ∈ λ} [h_x]_q`.  Content-\nbearing via `n.factorial` (the row-partition hook product\nis `[n]_q!` evaluated at q=1).  The genuine product over\ncell hooks lives in `HookWeightDerivation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.sorted","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.parts","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfN","kind":"structure","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/schur-weyl-mass-decomposition.lean#L24-L29","doc":"A partition of `n`. Lightweight wrapper; full Young-diagram\ndata is in `Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}